WEBVTT

00:00.031 --> 00:10.023
[SPEAKER_00]: Nighttime on the 6th of Whale Sun, probably around 10pm in the morning, the party sits above on the beach.

00:14.656 --> 00:27.166
[SPEAKER_00]: On the rocky cliffs, not very high rocky cliffs, you're probably, I would say, maybe 30 feet above where the wharf is, looking down on the wharf that Owen Black piloted the smuggling sloop into.

00:28.788 --> 00:30.689
[SPEAKER_00]: So the four of you are basically sitting there.

00:32.591 --> 00:34.212
[SPEAKER_00]: It's going to be midnight soon.

00:37.139 --> 00:38.940
[SPEAKER_00]: You guys want to have a conversation about things?

00:38.960 --> 00:40.282
[SPEAKER_00]: We left it lit, right?

00:40.302 --> 00:41.102
[SPEAKER_00]: We left it lit.

00:41.122 --> 00:49.209
[SPEAKER_00]: You left two lanterns on, one on the wharf and one actually on the mast of the ship so you could see anybody that was coming on.

00:49.849 --> 01:03.180
[SPEAKER_00]: You're about, I would say, 150 feet away, probably just right in short bow range for a long bow.

01:03.200 --> 01:03.941
[SPEAKER_00]: Okay.

01:04.931 --> 01:08.593
[SPEAKER_00]: It's long range for a crossbow.

01:09.413 --> 01:12.935
[SPEAKER_00]: Somebody on the docks would be within 130 feet.

01:13.295 --> 01:17.637
[SPEAKER_00]: If you get onto the sloop, they would be at extreme range.

01:17.677 --> 01:19.558
[SPEAKER_00]: You shoot at disadvantage.

01:19.858 --> 01:21.619
[SPEAKER_00]: Two dice, you take the worst.

01:22.580 --> 01:24.100
[SPEAKER_00]: I've got used for

01:30.440 --> 01:32.281
[SPEAKER_02]: Eight-sided resting on Hill.

01:32.902 --> 01:34.563
[SPEAKER_02]: So I had to keep track of that.

01:34.703 --> 01:36.605
[SPEAKER_02]: That was my rest.

01:36.645 --> 01:42.649
[SPEAKER_04]: You can have three short rests a day, but all the dice only recover after a long rest.

01:42.970 --> 01:43.370
[SPEAKER_01]: Correct.

01:44.991 --> 01:46.152
[SPEAKER_01]: Can I do a short rest?

01:46.172 --> 01:47.533
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm only down two hit points.

01:48.594 --> 01:50.816
[SPEAKER_01]: Actually, I don't even know if I need to.

01:50.976 --> 01:53.458
[SPEAKER_03]: He played a song to give you one back.

01:55.329 --> 01:56.490
[SPEAKER_03]: No, you roll for your own.

01:56.510 --> 01:57.691
[SPEAKER_03]: You get a one die six.

01:58.091 --> 02:00.794
[SPEAKER_01]: I think we did that.

02:00.834 --> 02:02.396
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm good, I'm only down two.

02:03.497 --> 02:04.658
[SPEAKER_03]: I'm back to full health.

02:04.718 --> 02:06.320
[SPEAKER_03]: I used four of my dies.

02:06.620 --> 02:10.465
[SPEAKER_03]: Yeah, I'm back to full as well.

02:10.505 --> 02:12.367
[SPEAKER_02]: But I gotta keep track of that four that I used.

02:13.598 --> 02:16.599
[SPEAKER_04]: Until you take one rest, then you erase all of them.

02:16.739 --> 02:29.122
[SPEAKER_04]: Because you can take up to three short rests a day, and you have three more dice, one ten-sided and two eight-sideds, that you can use to recover hit points.

02:29.762 --> 02:35.124
[SPEAKER_04]: So in other words, if you get wounded a little bit, you can just use it until you recover.

02:35.624 --> 02:38.464
[SPEAKER_04]: But after you do three short rests, you have to take a long rest.

02:38.624 --> 02:40.505
[SPEAKER_01]: And then I believe we were going to go...

02:41.624 --> 02:42.546
[SPEAKER_01]: I can't remember.

02:42.767 --> 02:45.435
[SPEAKER_01]: Are we going to go down the beach or something?

02:45.455 --> 02:48.082
[SPEAKER_01]: Because Owen Black was somewhere, or am I tripping?

02:48.263 --> 02:49.667
[SPEAKER_01]: Well, let's have a conversation.

02:50.550 --> 02:54.341
[SPEAKER_01]: You guys are probably wanting to talk to Folsom about what's happening.

